  "note": "Election of the Downpatrick Urban District Council, polled Monday 15 May 1939 (Belfast News-Letter, 16 May 1939, p. 11, and Irish News, 16 May 1939, p. 5). Fourteen candidates for twelve seats; Nationalists six, Unionists five, Labour one (a Labour gain). Poll over 86 per cent. The Irish News prints the same figures but labels Perry 'Nat.'; the Belfast News-Letter's 'Lab.' matches its statement that Labour gained a seat. Citation unconfirmed: the names were not all found on the cited page (verification 5 Nov 2026)."
